Create a continuous floor, properly aligned walls, a coherent ceiling, correctly fitted doorways, connected corridors, and appropriately positioned equipment.

The interior should have consistent dimensions and realistic proportions. The player must be able to navigate through every intended passage without getting trapped between objects.

Design the locomotive cabin and carriage interiors around their actual gameplay purposes. Include functional space for driving, fuel handling, storage, repairs, crafting, resting, and other existing systems as appropriate.

Ensure that:

