2. Medium-distance trees using efficient models and instancing.
3. Distant forests represented with suitable low-detail geometry and stable density.

Coordinate wind animation across all LOD levels.

Do not generate identical trees at regular intervals or fill every square metre with vegetation.

Include believable clearings, valleys, wetlands, rocky outcrops, and other ecological transitions.

Forests must blend naturally into the surrounding terrain rather than forming obvious rectangular biome boundaries.

